@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080
@employeeId = 1

### Create an employee. Use the returned ID below.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/employees
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Ananya Rao",
  "email": "ananya.rao@example.com",
  "phoneNumber": "+91 98765 43210",
  "department": "ENGINEERING",
  "designation": "Backend Engineer",
  "dateOfJoining": "2024-07-01",
  "salary": 650000.50,
  "status": "ACTIVE"
}

### List with search, combined filters and pagination
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/employees?search=ananya&department=ENGINEERING&status=ACTIVE&page=0&size=10&sortBy=fullName&direction=asc

### Get one employee
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/employees/{{employeeId}}

### Update all editable fields
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/employees/{{employeeId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Ananya Rao",
  "email": "ananya.rao@example.com",
  "phoneNumber": "+91 98765 43210",
  "department": "ENGINEERING",
  "designation": "Software Engineer",
  "dateOfJoining": "2024-07-01",
  "salary": 700000,
  "status": "ACTIVE"
}

### Directory-wide totals
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/employees/summary

### Delete the example employee permanently
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/employees/{{employeeId}}

### Invalid page size: expect 400
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/employees?size=101

### Missing employee: expect 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/employees/9223372036854775807
